Klipolo capture

Files derived from Cap's MIT-licensed `scap-*` and `cap-camera*` crates (https://github.com/CapSoftware/Cap),
commit d327051c175aa092c06ad9fc6684298b1b5fed6b, Copyright (c) 2023-present Cap Software, Inc., are used under the
MIT licence (its text ships as `Cap-MIT.txt` in the app's licences). Each starts `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`
and names its crate:
  src/vendor/cap/sck/capture.rs: from crates/scap-screencapturekit/src/capture.rs (scap-screencapturekit)
  src/vendor/cap/sck/config.rs: from crates/scap-screencapturekit/src/config.rs (scap-screencapturekit)
  src/vendor/cap/sck/mod.rs: from crates/scap-screencapturekit/src/lib.rs (scap-screencapturekit; its two modules)
  src/platform/macos/camera.rs: from crates/camera-avfoundation/src/lib.rs (cap-camera-avfoundation; the sample-buffer
    delegate), with the session set-up and teardown of crates/camera/src/macos.rs (cap-camera)

Files derived from other Cap crates, at the same commit, Copyright (c) 2023-present Cap Software, Inc., are used under
the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 (AGPL-3.0), the licence Klipolo is distributed under (LICENSE at the
repository root):
  src/probe/ladder.rs: from crates/enc-ffmpeg/src/video/h264.rs (the Windows encoder ladders and the live options,
    copied as data by hand); its Linux ladder and `vaapi`/`vulkan` options are Klipolo's own
  src/hosttime.rs: from crates/timestamp/src/macos.rs and crates/timestamp/src/win.rs (`from_cpal`, adapted by hand
    to the host clock in ns); its re-base follows the design of crates/recording/src/sources/capture_clock.rs

Each file names its Cap source path and lists Klipolo's changes in its header. Sources whose design only was taken (no
code) are cited in the files that follow them.

The crates the recorder's OS backends add (cpal, cidre, objc2, tray-icon, global-hotkey) are listed, with their
licences, in the app's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
